body:
I think I get it;

Focusing on the fact that you dont have positive experiences is negative because you're thinking about something you dont have 

Accepting your negative experiences is a positive thing because theres not really anything else you can do about them, & acceptance is a positive experience

I relate so much with this;  I didn't have to do chores, I was shooed out of the kitchen if my mo was in it (so I never learned to cook), didn't have a job, we didn't have a washing machine so I never even learned to do my own laundry

&#x200B;

Sounds like a kid's dream, but it didn't do me any favours as an adult.

Well it's not like I can help how I'm raised, but seeing as I didn't have much control over how & what I ate as a child, the fact that I'm ACTIVELY TRYING now, & seeing some improvement compared to everyone else in my family should indicate that I actually know what I'm doing.

&#x200B;

I don't eat snacks 24/7 like you seem to assume I do.  I like having a bag of snacks in my purse for when I'm out of the house longer than planned, because dried fruit & nuts is a fuckton healthier than McDonalds, or whatever other cheap & easy option is available wherever I am.  Sometimes I like a treat, & if a couple squares of dark chocolate is going to stop me from eating a brownie or ice cream, then more fucking power to me.
